rTest.java $T/CheckoutGuestE2ETest.java $T/pages/ReviewPage.java; ls $T $T/pages; cat src/main/resources/templates/checkout/review.pug","description":"Read e2e harness and pages"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01PCxfgdkrWwpa4DYMtpH5Kr","tool_input":{"command":"cd /Users/christoph/Privat/domain-centric-architecture/dca-ecommerce-sample-java/src/main/resources/templates && grep -n \"checkout/start\\|cartId\" cart/*.pug; grep -n \"input\\|select\\|form\" checkout/delivery.pug | head -40; sed -n 60,110p ../../java/dev/domaincentric/sample/ecommerce/checkout/adapter/incoming/web/checkoutcompletion/ReviewPageController.java","description":"Inspect cart and delivery forms"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01Qa7DiBRLwG8PZF2iZr8iVu","tool_input":{"command":"find src/main -name CheckoutRoutes.java -exec cat {} \\; ; grep -rn \"parallel\" src/test*/resources gradle/plugins/*.gradle 2>/dev/null","description":"Read CheckoutRoutes and check parallel config"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_014dQ2rfQSZgBmiKayQqMt6F","tool_input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\np='src/test-e2e/java/dev/domaincentric/sample/ecommerce/e2e/ShopUnderTest.java'\ns=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace(\"import com.github.tomakehurst.wiremock.WireMockServer;\\n\",\"import com.github.tomakehurst.wiremock.WireMockServer;\\nimport com.github.tomakehurst.wiremock.client.ResponseDefinitionBuilder;\\n\")\ns=s.replace(\"public static com.github.tomakehurst.wiremock.client.ResponseDefinitionBuilder authorized()\",\"public static ResponseDefinitionBuilder authorized()\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF","description":"Import ResponseDefinitionBuilder in ShopUnderTest"}}],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":35,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"The test stage for `pay-through-the-provider` is finished. All three acceptance criteria have a test, and each one compiles and fails on its own assertion, not on missing code or a setup error. No production code or build files were changed.\n\n| Criterion | Test | How it fails today |\n|---|---|---|\n| authorized-payment-moves-to-review | `ProviderPaymentE2ETest#authorizedPaymentMovesTheCheckoutToReview` (browser) | \"the payment provider received one payment request\" — expected 1, got 0 |\n| refused-payment-stays-at-payment | `ProviderPaymentIntegrationTest#refusedPaymentKeepsTheCustomerAtThePaymentStep` | the checkout moves on to `/checkout/review` instead of staying at `/checkout/payment` |\n| slow-provider-counts-as-unavailable | `ProviderPaymentIntegrationTest#slowProviderCountsAsUnavailable` | same as the refused case |\n\nThey fail because the shop still pays through the built-in stand-in, which never contacts a provider.\n\n- **Integration tests:** they walk a guest checkout through the real pages up to the payment step, with a WireMock stub standing in for the provider. I added two more that aren't in the criteria table: the provider answering with a server error (`500`), and the provider dropping the connection. Both expect the \"not available\" message.\n- **Browser suite:** the shop the suite starts now comes with its own provider stub, which approves every payment unless a test sets up another answer. When the suite runs against a shop started elsewhere, there's no stub to control, so the new test skips. I ran the whole browser suite with this change: 23 tests, the new one fails as intended, and one test skips, the same one as before.\n- **Other checks:** the formatter has been run.\n\nThe build stage needs to know two things (both are in `tasks/pay-through-the-provider/tests.md`):\n- **Total on the review page:** the browser test reads it through `data-test=\"review-total\"`. That attribute is part of the plan's template changes and doesn't exist yet. It isn't hit today only because the request-count check fails first.\n- **Provider address setting:** the tests use the plan's working name `checkout.payment-provider.base-url`. If the build stage picks a different name, it has to change it in both test files.\n\nI didn't write unit tests. The plan names no aggregate or value-object rules, and how the use case handles an unavailable provider is covered by the integration tests. I also didn't run the story gate, since this stage only writes the tests.","ttft_ms":7416,"type":"result","duration_ms":402528,"uuid":"7ca9a0ea-ee6f-41f8-9515-476c9423ea2e","ttft_stream_ms":6139,"time_to_request_ms":43,"first_content_frame_ms":6140,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
